{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 63, :comments ["<b>And Yitzhak went out.</b> From where did he go out? From Garden of Eden, where he was there from the time of the Binding (Akedah) until now — three years." "<b>La-suach in the field.</b> From the root of שיח השדה (field shrubs): under one of the shrubs, that is, to plant trees and to oversee the affairs of his workers. Another interpretation: from the root of שיחה (conversation) — to speak with the man he needed to speak with."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:05:42.368488042Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}